<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19475" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gĕnŭīnus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj.
		geno, gigno, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>innate</i>, <i>native</i>, <i>natural.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b> (rare but class.): genuinae
			domesticaeque virtutes, * <i><span class="en">Cic. Rep.
				2, 15, 29</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">naturales et genuini honores,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell.
					2, 2, 9</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pietas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig. 43, 28, 3, § 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nequitia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 9, p. 230</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>genuine</i>, <i>authentic</i> (post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">comoedia Plauti,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell.
					3, 3, 7</span></i>
			. 
			</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
